IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-definitions-products`
IMPORT `sfa-associates`
IMPORT `sfab-division-1`
IMPORT `sfab-insider-1`
IMPORT `sfab-insider-2`
IMPORT `sfab-insider-3`
IMPORT `sfab-civil`
IMPORT `sfab-attributed`

-- Integration tests: a keel function (section 2(1), section 3(1)) or another sfab function feeds a MAYBE BOOLEAN input of a function in this part.
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the sections named. The keel's `s 3(1)` takes: the context flag, limbs (a) to (g), and the answer under s 3(3).
-- Reading the arguments of `s 3(1)` below: `FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE)` is a person
-- who is a director of the other person's corporation (limb (a) is JUST TRUE) and in no other way associated.

-- s 3(1)(a): a director of the corporation is associated with it, so the keel answers JUST TRUE.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No limb holds: the keel answers JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The context requires a different meaning: the keel answers NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 197(3)(b): an offer to sell, and the person knows another person has made an offer to buy: the presumption arises only if that other person is associated.
#ASSERT `s 197(3)(b) the person's purpose is presumed by reason of an offer to sell matched by an offer to purchase` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 197(3)(b) the person's purpose is presumed by reason of an offer to sell matched by an offer to purchase` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 197(3)(b) the person's purpose is presumed by reason of an offer to sell matched by an offer to purchase` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 230(1): an unsolicited transaction for a principal is no contravention unless the principal is an associate of the holder.
#ASSERT `s 230(1) the holder or representative does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by an unsolicited transaction for a principal` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 230(1) the holder or representative does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by an unsolicited transaction for a principal` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 230(1) the holder or representative does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by an unsolicited transaction for a principal` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 196A(b): a securities-based derivatives contract of the corporation, through the keel's section 2(1) definition.
#ASSERT `s 196A(b) the contract is a securities-based derivatives contract of the corporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196A(b) the contract is a securities-based derivatives contract of the corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 218(5)(b), s 215 and s 218(1): a director possesses information that is not generally available and is expected to move the price: subsection (2) applies to the director.
#ASSERT `s 218(1) subsections (2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) apply to the connected person` (`s 218(5)(b) the person is connected to the corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE (`s 215 the information is generally available` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`s 216 a reasonable person would be taken to expect the information to have a material effect on the price or value` TRUE FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same information once it is readily observable (s 215): generally available, so the connected person is not caught.
#ASSERT `s 218(1) subsections (2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) apply to the connected person` (`s 218(5)(b) the person is connected to the corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE (`s 215 the information is generally available` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`s 216 a reasonable person would be taken to expect the information to have a material effect on the price or value` TRUE FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An outsider with no access (no limb of s 218(5)(b)) is not a connected person: s 218(1) answers JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 218(1) subsections (2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) apply to the connected person` (`s 218(5)(b) the person is connected to the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE (`s 215 the information is generally available` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`s 216 a reasonable person would be taken to expect the information to have a material effect on the price or value` TRUE FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 218(2) fed by s 218(1): the connected person who sold while the information was not generally available contravenes subsection (2).
#ASSERT `s 218(2) the connected person's dealing or procuring contravenes the bar` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 221(1) fed by s 218(2): a contravention of s 218(2) makes the person guilty of an offence.
#ASSERT `s 221(1) the person is guilty of an offence` (`s 218(2) the connected person's dealing or procuring contravenes the bar` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 234(1) fed by s 218(2): the contravening person who gained a profit is liable to a claimant who dealt contemporaneously and lost.
#ASSERT `s 234(1) the contravening person is liable to pay compensation to the claimant` (`s 218(2) the connected person's dealing or procuring contravenes the bar` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE) TRUE (`s 234(1)(a) the claimant had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention` TRUE) (`s 234(1)(b) the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference in price` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- and a claimant whose loss was not shown (s 234(1)(b) NOTHING) leaves the answer NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 234(1) the contravening person is liable to pay compensation to the claimant` (`s 218(2) the connected person's dealing or procuring contravenes the bar` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE) TRUE (`s 234(1)(a) the claimant had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention` TRUE) (`s 234(1)(b) the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference in price` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 202(1) fed by s 202(2): the circulation contravenes if a condition of subsection (2) holds.
#ASSERT `s 202(1) the person's circulation of a statement or information contravenes the bar on disseminating information about illegal transactions` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`s 202(2) a condition in subsection (1) is satisfied` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 202(1) the person's circulation of a statement or information contravenes the bar on disseminating information about illegal transactions` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`s 202(2) a condition in subsection (1) is satisfied` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 232(2) and (3): the highest penalty is the greater of 3 times the profit and $2 million; the lowest is $100,000 for a corporation and $50,000 for anyone else.
-- Profit $1,000,000 gives 3 times = $3,000,000, which exceeds $2 million.
#ASSERT `s 232(2) the highest civil penalty the court may order` (`s 232(2)(a) three times the profit gained or the loss avoided` 1000000 0) `s 232(2)(b) the fixed amount in the cap` EQUALS 3000000
#ASSERT `s 232(2) and (3) the civil penalty ordered is within the limits` 3000000 (`s 232(2) the highest civil penalty the court may order` (`s 232(2)(a) three times the profit gained or the loss avoided` 1000000 0) `s 232(2)(b) the fixed amount in the cap`) (`s 232(3) the lowest civil penalty the court may order` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 232(2) and (3) the civil penalty ordered is within the limits` 3000001 (`s 232(2) the highest civil penalty the court may order` (`s 232(2)(a) three times the profit gained or the loss avoided` 1000000 0) `s 232(2)(b) the fixed amount in the cap`) (`s 232(3) the lowest civil penalty the court may order` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Profit $100,000 gives 3 times = $300,000, below $2 million: the cap is $2 million.
#ASSERT `s 232(2) the highest civil penalty the court may order` (`s 232(2)(a) three times the profit gained or the loss avoided` 100000 0) `s 232(2)(b) the fixed amount in the cap` EQUALS 2000000
-- An individual's floor is $50,000: $60,000 is within the limits, $49,999 is not.
#ASSERT `s 232(2) and (3) the civil penalty ordered is within the limits` 60000 2000000 (`s 232(3) the lowest civil penalty the court may order` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 232(2) and (3) the civil penalty ordered is within the limits` 49999 2000000 (`s 232(3) the lowest civil penalty the court may order` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 234(6) feeds s 234(2): profit $500,000 less $100,000 already ordered is a ceiling of $400,000; a claimant's loss of $450,000 with $20,000 already paid is capped at $400,000.
#ASSERT `s 234(2) the amount of compensation under subsection (1)` 450000 20000 (`s 234(6) the maximum recoverable amount` 500000 0 100000) EQUALS 400000

-- s 236(4) and s 236(1): a conviction not subject to further appeal is made final, so the court may fix a date.
#ASSERT `s 236(1) the relevant court may fix a date on or before which all claimants have to file and prove their claims` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`s 236(4) the conviction is made final` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 236(1) the relevant court may fix a date on or before which all claimants have to file and prove their claims` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`s 236(4) the conviction is made final` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 236A and s 236D(1): a corporation liable under s 236C(1) is a defendant corporation, and then owes compensation to a claimant who dealt contemporaneously and lost.
#ASSERT `s 236D(1) the corporation is liable to pay compensation to the claimant` (`s 236A "defendant corporation" a corporation liable under section 236B or 236C` FALSE TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 236D(1) the corporation is liable to pay compensation to the claimant` (`s 236A "defendant corporation" a corporation liable under section 236B or 236C` FALSE FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
